  "cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "guest.fdlock.orphans",
      "behavior": "the unchanged control descriptor reads its bytes; an unlinked descriptor keeps its file; an orphan truncates through its node; directory scans preserve orphan handles; a refused rename preserves both nodes; an orphan remains readable in another process; process exit releases orphan references; a relocation updates another process descriptor; directory removal respects descriptors and working directories; duplicates retain an orphan until their last close; growth relocates all open descriptions; repeated close releases orphans; unheld unlinks do not leak nodes; replacement without a holder does not leak nodes",
